BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Replay buttons (luaui/widgets/gui_replaybuttons.lua): the speed column above the app's
dock. BAR puts the column (skip or pause, then 0.5x to 20x) at the screen's left edge from 14.5 % of its height up; the
app's dock, upright a third to a half of the height, lay over all but the fastest speeds, 1x among them (dev phone,
2026-11-15, a replay spectated upright at the unfolded Fold7's 1080x1198: 4x the lowest in sight). Where the dock lies
under the column it starts just above the dock's top; back at BAR's place when the dock goes (sideways pinned to the
right, folded away by HIDE, no dock). The file is the same in every BAR release on the dev phone (test-31465 to
test-31958), so this fits replays of all of them. Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI
loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.

@@@ find
function widget:Update(dt)
	prevIsActive = isActive
	isActive = #Spring.GetSelectedUnits() == 0
end
@@@ with
function widget:Update(dt)
	prevIsActive = isActive
	isActive = #Spring.GetSelectedUnits() == 0
	-- BAR Droid (phone): the column above the app's dock where the dock lies under it
	local droidP = WG.BarDroidPortrait
	local dock = droidP and droidP.active and droidP.active() and droidP.dock and droidP.dock() or nil
	local base = 0.145
	if dock and dock[1] <= bWidth * vsx then
		base = math.max(base, (dock[4] + 8) / vsy)
	end
	if #buttons > 0 and buttons[#buttons].y ~= base then
		local dy = 0
		for i = 1, #speeds do
			dy = dy + bHeight
			buttons[i].y = base + dy
		end
		buttons[#buttons].y = base
		wPos.y = base
		sceduleUpdate = true
	end
end
@@@ end
